# Whippoorwill's effects are about the creature it targeted, and only for the turn (CR 611.2a, 514.2). On turn 3 Bot1 activates
# it on Bot2's Drudge Skeletons; Bot2 then bolts Whippoorwill, and Bot1's Healing Salve prevents that damage: damage to another
# creature can still be prevented that turn. On turn 5 Bot1 bolts the Skeletons and Bot2's Healing Salve prevents it all, then
# bolts them again and Bot2 regenerates them: both effects have ended, so the Skeletons are unhurt, then destroyed and
# regenerated (tapped, CR 701.19a), never dying.

